IMPORT prelude

-- Government Securities (Debt Market and Investment) Act 1992 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a holder of Singapore
-- Government securities, Treasury Bills or advance deposits, and for a financial institution that deals in them: which instruments
-- are "Government securities" (s 2), the borrowing and RMGS ceilings (ss 11, 15A, 15B), transfers and pledges of book-entry
-- securities (ss 18A, 19, 20(4), 21), interest and redemption (ss 23, 24, 24A), advance deposits (ss 27, 28), and primary
-- dealers -- appointment, the offence of dealing unappointed, orders, appeals and inspection (ss 29A, 29B, 29D, 29E, 29F) -- with
-- the offence ceilings for the regulations (s 31(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GSDMIA1992.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the text also
-- carries annotations for Act 35 of 2021 (wef 31/01/2022) and, the latest annotated, Act 5 of 2022 (wef 21/02/2022), which added
-- Part 3A (RMGS). The deposit's metadata records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. REQ-0113 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a holder, depositor, pledgee or dealer meets. Not encoded: the Government Securities Fund
-- and its accounting (ss 3 to 10, 12, 13, 15, 15C), securities lending (s 11A) beyond its effect on redemption, the Authority's
-- record-keeping powers (ss 18, 22), conditions and directions to primary dealers beyond the notice period (ss 29B(1)-(3), (5),
-- (6), 29C), the financial-penalty formula (s 29D(3), which is in a Gazette notification not deposited), and the regulations.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Government Securities (Debt Market and Investment) Act 1992 -- holders and dealers`

DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `a Government bond`
    `a Treasury Bill`
    `an RMGS`
    `an advance deposit`

§§ `2, 14, 15B, 23, 24, 27 -- what kind of instrument it is`

-- s 2: "Government securities" means any stock, bond, note, certificate or similar instruments issued under this Act "other than any
-- Treasury Bill and any RMGS". s 23(1): interest on Government securities "must be paid half-yearly". s 24(1): Government securities
-- "are redeemable at par". s 15B(1): every RMGS "is redeemable at par only". s 27(4): "Interest on advance deposits must be paid
-- half-yearly". s 14: a Treasury Bill has a maturity "ordinarily not exceeding one year" and its repayment conditions are left to
-- the regulations and the Minister -- the Act itself fixes neither interest nor par redemption for it.
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is a Government security` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `a Government bond` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act requires half-yearly interest` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `a Government bond` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an advance deposit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act makes it redeemable at par` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `a Government bond` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an RMGS` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 15A(5): "RMGS must not be issued to a person other than the Authority." s 15B(2)(a): an RMGS "is not transferable without the
-- consent of the Minister".
GIVEN `the recipient is the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an RMGS may be issued to the recipient` IF
    `the recipient is the Authority`

§§ `11, 15A -- the ceilings`

-- s 11(2): the Minister "must not raise a loan" if the aggregate borrowed by Government securities and Treasury Bills and
-- outstanding at any time "exceeds $1,065,000,000,000, or any higher amount specified in a resolution of Parliament with which the
-- President concurs". s 15A(2): RMGS issued and not redeemed "must not at any time exceed $580,000,000,000", or a higher amount so
-- specified. Amounts here are in BILLIONS of dollars; a `higher amount` of 0 means no resolution.
GIVEN `statutory ceiling` IS A NUMBER, `higher amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `higher amount` GREATER THAN `statutory ceiling` THEN `higher amount` ELSE `statutory ceiling`

GIVEN `outstanding after the loan` IS A NUMBER, `higher amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may raise the loan` IF
    `outstanding after the loan` AT MOST `the larger of` 1065 `higher amount`

GIVEN `RMGS unredeemed after the issue` IS A NUMBER, `higher amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the RMGS may be issued` IF
    `RMGS unredeemed after the issue` AT MOST `the larger of` 580 `higher amount`

§§ `18A, 19, 20, 21 -- transfers and pledges of book-entry securities`

-- s 18A: a holder "may transfer or pledge" book-entry Government securities "except where the transfer or pledge is prohibited in,
-- or is not in accordance with, the terms of the issue".
GIVEN `prohibited by the terms of issue` IS A BOOLEAN, `not in accordance with the terms of issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder may transfer or pledge` IF
    (NOT `prohibited by the terms of issue`) AND (NOT `not in accordance with the terms of issue`)

DECLARE Method IS ONE OF
    `by entry in the Authority's records`
    `by other means`

-- s 19(3): a transfer or pledge effected by entry in the Authority's records "has priority over any transfer or pledge involving, or
-- any interest in, the security effected or created in any other manner before, on or after the date" of the entry. The Act does
-- not rank two claims made the same way; the rule below answers only whether s 19(3) gives the first claim priority.
GIVEN `the first claim` IS A Method, `the second claim` IS A Method
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(3) gives the first claim priority` IF
    CONSIDER `the first claim`
    WHEN `by entry in the Authority's records` THEN
        CONSIDER `the second claim`
        WHEN `by other means` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 20(1): a transfer or pledge "may be effected by any means" that would work for certificated securities; but s 20(4): the Authority
-- "must not accept any notice or advice of a transfer or pledge ... not effected in accordance with section 19 and any such notice or
-- advice is void".
GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Method
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notice of the transfer to the Authority is void` IF
    CONSIDER `the transfer`
    WHEN `by other means` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 21(1): the Authority "is not liable for conversion or for participation in any breach of fiduciary duty" where it acted
-- "according to the instructions of its depositor even if the depositor had no right to dispose of" the securities.
GIVEN `acted on the depositor's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN, `the depositor had the right to dispose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21 protects the Authority from liability for conversion` IF
    `acted on the depositor's instructions`

§§ `23, 24, 24A -- interest and redemption`

-- s 24(1): Government securities are redeemable at par (a) on the date of maturity; or (b) where "redeemable at the election of the
-- holder thereof at any time, on the earlier of" the date of maturity and the redemption date in a notice of intention to redeem
-- "duly served in the prescribed manner". Days are counted as day numbers.
GIVEN `holder may elect to redeem` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice duly served` IS A BOOLEAN, `maturity day` IS A NUMBER, `notice redemption day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the redemption day` MEANS
    IF `holder may elect to redeem` AND `notice duly served` AND `notice redemption day` LESS THAN `maturity day`
    THEN `notice redemption day`
    ELSE `maturity day`

-- s 24(3): after the date of maturity "all the interest on the principal sums payable on the Government securities ceases and
-- determines, whether or not payment of the principal sums has been demanded".
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `maturity day` IS A NUMBER, `principal demanded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `interest runs on the day` IF
    `the day` AT MOST `maturity day`

-- s 23(2): where a holder-redeemable security is redeemed before maturity, "a portion of the half-yearly interest payable on that
-- Government security (calculated on a pro-rata basis)" is payable on the redemption date. INFERENCE: the Act does not say pro rata
-- to what; days elapsed over days in the half-year is assumed.
GIVEN `half-yearly interest` IS A NUMBER, `days elapsed` IS A NUMBER, `days in the half-year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pro-rata interest` MEANS
    `half-yearly interest` TIMES `days elapsed` DIVIDED BY `days in the half-year`

-- s 24(2): securities "held by the Authority for the purpose of securities lending to primary dealers under section 11A" are
-- redeemable "on such conditions as are agreed upon between the Government and the Authority" -- not at par under s 24(1).
GIVEN `held by the Authority for securities lending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 24(1) par redemption applies` IF
    NOT `held by the Authority for securities lending`

-- s 24A(1): the Authority may "by public notice invite the public to apply to redeem" securities before maturity; (3) it "may refuse
-- any application ... without giving any reason". So only a holder-redeemable security with a duly served notice (s 24(1)(b)) gives
-- the holder a right to early redemption; an application under a s 24A invitation does not.
GIVEN `holder may elect to redeem` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice duly served` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied under a s 24A invitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder can require redemption before maturity` IF
    `holder may elect to redeem` AND `notice duly served`

§§ `27, 28 -- advance deposits`

-- s 27(2): advance deposits carry interest "calculated from the date the deposit was effectively received"; (3) "where cheques for
-- the advance deposits cannot be cleared on the day of receipt, interest is to be calculated from the next working day".
GIVEN `day received` IS A NUMBER, `cheque not cleared that day` IS A BOOLEAN, `next working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day interest starts` MEANS
    IF `cheque not cleared that day` THEN `next working day` ELSE `day received`

-- s 27(6): a depositor wanting repayment "must give at least 2 working days' notice to the Authority".
GIVEN `working days of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the repayment notice is sufficient` IF
    `working days of notice` AT LEAST 2

-- s 28: "Any power to invest conferred on a person by any instrument or other written law is, unless the contrary intention appears
-- ... deemed to include power to make advance deposits".
GIVEN `has a power to invest` IS A BOOLEAN, `contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the investor may make advance deposits` IF
    `has a power to invest` AND (NOT `contrary intention appears`)

§§ `29A -- primary dealers`

-- s 29A(1): the business is (a) applying to the Authority to purchase Government securities, Treasury Bills or public debt securities
-- "on behalf of another person" under a public invitation, or (b) offering to redeem them on behalf of another person. (6): a person
-- "who is not a primary dealer" who "carries on or holds himself, herself or itself out as carrying on or willing to carry on" that
-- business is guilty of an offence. s 31(1)(g): regulations may exempt a financial institution from Part 7A.
GIVEN `is a primary dealer` IS A BOOLEAN, `carries on or holds out the business` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dealing without appointment is an offence` IF
    (NOT `is a primary dealer`) AND `carries on or holds out the business` AND (NOT `exempted by regulations`)

-- s 29A(4): the Authority "may refuse an application" if (a) required information is not provided; (b) the applicant does not meet,
-- or is unlikely to continue to meet, prescribed requirements; or (c) a statement or document is "false or misleading in any material
-- particular". (Refusal on the s 29A(2) considerations -- financial standing, experience, public interest -- is not modelled.)
GIVEN `information withheld` IS A BOOLEAN, `requirements not met` IS A BOOLEAN, `materially false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may refuse the application` IF
    `information withheld` OR `requirements not met` OR `materially false or misleading`

§§ `29A(6), 29F(6), 31(3) -- penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `dealing without appointment`
    `failing an inspection requirement`
    `breaching the regulations`

-- s 29A(6): (a) an individual -- fine "not exceeding $125,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or ... both", and
-- "$12,500 for every day" of a continuing offence after conviction; (b) any other case -- "$250,000" and "$25,000" a day.
-- s 29F(6): "any person" who without reasonable excuse fails to produce books or explain them -- "$50,000 or ... imprisonment for a term
-- not exceeding 2 years or ... both", and "$5,000" a day; the subsection does not distinguish individuals.
-- s 31(3): regulations may make a contravention punishable (a) for an individual with "$12,500 or ... 12 months or ... both" and
-- "$1,250" a day; (b) otherwise "$25,000" and "$2,500" a day.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `dealing without appointment` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 125000 ELSE 250000
    WHEN `failing an inspection requirement` THEN 50000
    WHEN `breaching the regulations` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 12500 ELSE 25000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `dealing without appointment` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 12500 ELSE 25000
    WHEN `failing an inspection requirement` THEN 5000
    WHEN `breaching the regulations` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 1250 ELSE 2500

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `dealing without appointment` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 36 ELSE 0
    WHEN `failing an inspection requirement` THEN 24
    WHEN `breaching the regulations` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 12 ELSE 0

-- s 29F(6): the offence is failing "without reasonable excuse" to comply with s 29F(2) or a requirement under s 29F(5).
GIVEN `failed to produce or explain` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing the inspection is an offence` IF
    `failed to produce or explain` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `29B, 29D, 29E -- conditions, orders and appeals`

-- s 29B(4)(c): before modifying a dealer's conditions the Authority must give notice specifying a time "being at least 28 days from
-- the date of service" for written representations -- "unless the Authority in respect of any particular case considers that it is
-- not practicable or desirable to do so".
GIVEN `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER, `Authority considers notice impracticable or undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the modification notice complies` IF
    `Authority considers notice impracticable or undesirable` OR `days allowed for representations` AT LEAST 28

DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `a cancellation`
    `a suspension`
    `a reprimand`
    `a financial penalty`

-- s 29D(2)(a): in lieu of cancellation the Authority may "suspend the appointment for such period (not exceeding 6 months)".
GIVEN `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension period is permitted` IF
    `months of suspension` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months of suspension` AT MOST 6

-- s 29D(5): no order unless the dealer had an opportunity of being heard "being a period of at least 21 days but not more than 28
-- days".
GIVEN `days given to be heard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hearing period is valid` IF
    `days given to be heard` AT LEAST 21 AND `days given to be heard` AT MOST 28

-- s 29D(7): an order "must not take effect until the expiry of 21 days after the Authority has served the notice of its order";
-- (9): a reprimand "takes effect on the date it is served". s 29E(2)(a): where an appeal is lodged a cancellation "does not take
-- effect unless the order is confirmed by the Minister or the appeal is ... dismissed ... or withdrawn"; (b) every other order
-- appealed against takes effect and must be complied with meanwhile. INFERENCE: "until the expiry of 21 days" is read as from the
-- 22nd day after service, counting the day of service as day 0.
GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order, `days since service` IS A NUMBER, `appeal pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is in effect` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `a reprimand` THEN `days since service` AT LEAST 0
    WHEN `a cancellation` THEN `days since service` GREATER THAN 21 AND (NOT `appeal pending`)
    OTHERWISE `days since service` GREATER THAN 21

-- s 29E(1): a dealer aggrieved by a condition, a direction or "any order of the Authority under section 29D(1), (2) or (3) except an
-- order of reprimand" may appeal to the Minister "within 14 days of the receipt" of it; the Minister's "decision is final".
GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order, `days since receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal lies to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `a reprimand` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `days since receipt` AT MOST 14
